{
  "description": "ADR-OWD-07 D-LAZY-8 (R31-HOT): a child's MCP grant when its parent holds a server whole (x.pipeshub.mcp[].tools: at_first_use, ADR-OWD-07 D-LAZY-2), whose tools the parent's tool grants name none of. One table for Node (domain/child-runs.ts childGrants + childRunSpec) and Python (harness_core.journal.children child_grants + child_spec). `parentSpec` is child-grants.json's with mcp-rovo held whole. `tools` is the checked grant (a server whole is `mcp@<instance>/*`), `childTools` the child spec's grants.tools, `mcp` its x.pipeshub.mcp. A child never holds more than its parent: a server held whole stays whole only when the request omits tools or names it whole; named tools of it are pinned to exactly those. R31HOT2 (ADR-OWD-07 D-LAZY-5): `pins` is what the parent's worker carries into the spawn (`mcpPins`), its first-use pins by instance; `parentSpecPins` sets `x.pipeshub.mcp[].pins` on the parent's own spec (a child that inherited a pin, spawning in turn). A child keeps the parent's pin narrowed to what it holds (`mcp[].pins`); a server held whole that the parent has listed holds only the tools its pin names; the spec's own pin wins over a carried one; a pin for a server the parent does not hold is never carried.",
